.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SCT_PRINT 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SCT_print ,
.Nm SCT_LIST_print ,
.Nm SCT_validation_status_string
.Nd Prints Signed Certificate Timestamps in a human-readable way
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Ft void
.Fo SCT_print
.Fa "const SCT *sct"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "int indent"
.Fa "const CTLOG_STORE *logs"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo SCT_LIST_print
.Fa "const STACK_OF(SCT) *sct_list"
.Fa "BIO *out"
.Fa "int indent"
.Fa "const char *separator"
.Fa "const CTLOG_STORE *logs"
.Fc
.Ft const char *
.Fo SCT_validation_status_string
.Fa "const SCT *sct"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SCT_print
prints a single Signed Certificate Timestamp (SCT) to a
.Vt BIO
in a human-readable format.
.Fn SCT_LIST_print
prints an entire list of SCTs in a similar way.
A separator can be specified to delimit each SCT in the output.
.Pp
The output can be indented by a specified number of spaces.
If a
.Sy CTLOG_STORE
is provided, it will be used to print the description of the CT log that
issued each SCT (if that log is in the CTLOG_STORE). Alternatively, NULL
can be passed as the CTLOG_STORE parameter to disable this feature.
.Pp
.Fn SCT_validation_status_string
will return the validation status of an SCT as a human-readable string.
Call
.Xr SCT_validate 3
or
.Xr SCT_LIST_validate 3
beforehand in order to set the validation status of an SCT first.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SCT_validation_status_string
returns a NUL-terminated string representing the validation status of an
.Sy SCT
object.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7 ,
.Xr bio 7 ,
.Xr CTLOG_STORE_new 3 ,
.Xr SCT_validate 3
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
